// E0206: a `Map` key type that is not ordered.
//
// `Map`'s iteration order is canonical — `map_keys` is ascending, always — and
// an order is only canonical if every key it holds has one. `Float` has none:
// `total_cmp` orders NaN and separates `0.0` from `-0.0`, and the language's
// `==` says NaN differs from itself and that the two zeros are one value. Either
// way a lookup would fail to find what it just inserted.
//
// Two shapes, one claim. The first names a concrete type; the second names a
// type parameter with no `where derivable(ord, k)` on its signature, which is
// the boundary the constraint belongs on.
//
// `derive` and constrained call sites are the other two shapes E0206 covers;
// they live in `not_derivable.ply`.

fn prices() -> Map<Float, String> = map_new()

fn index<k, v>(v: v) -> Map<k, v> = map_new()
